class.description:
Place it on (or as a child of) something that should know when the player looks at it: a monster that only moves while it is not watched, a painting that changes when looked away from, a hint that appears when stared at. It counts as watched when it is in view of the current [Camera3D], near the player's gaze (or anywhere on the screen, see [member detection_mode]), the player's eyes are open, and, with [member require_line_of_sight], nothing is in the way.
Without eye tracking running, the player counts as looking at the middle of the screen with open eyes, so the same scene works on machines without a webcam.
[codeblock]
# A monster that moves only while nobody watches it.
@onready var eyes_on_me: GazeTarget3D = $GazeTarget3D

func _physics_process(delta):
	if not eyes_on_me.is_watched():
		move_towards_player(delta)
[/codeblock]
